jobs.description:
Please note: at this point we only consider candidates currently based in the Netherlands.

At Schuberg Philis, we design, build, and maintain environments for our customers’ mission-critical applications, leveraging a blend of public cloud and on-premises infrastructures. Our dedicated customer teams are driven by ownership and have the ambition to always deliver the best results, regardless of complexity or constraints.

Are you as passionate about networking and automation as we are? We are looking for a Network Automation Engineer who thrives on designing, implementing and running advanced network solutions. Take ownership of critical network layers, integrate physical and virtual components and ensure seamless operation for our customers’ environment, both on-premises and in the cloud.

Automation is your default mindset. You will be focusing on designing and building a mission critical environment for our customers, engineered for high availability and stability. You and your team get to take full ownership of building as well as running and improving customer environments.

What will you be doing?

As a Network Automation Engineer, these activities will be part of your responsibility:
Architect, design, build and maintain highly available, secure, and scalable networks across on-premises and public cloud environments (e.g. Azure);
Automate and template network configurations (Infrastructure as Code) using tools such as Terraform, Chef, and Ansible;
Troubleshoot and remediate performance or security challenges across multifaceted network landscapes;
Manage and optimize logical and virtual networking solutions, including SDN and VMware NSX;
Integrate and manage IPAM (preferably Nautobot or Netbox) and IAM solutions, supporting an efficient and secure network environment;
Participate in Kubernetes networking, CI/CD automation, GitLab/GitOps workflows;
Prepare and support change planning, security incidents, audits and continuous network improvement;
Work on greenfield projects, with responsibility ranging from architecture to hands-on building and continuous development.

What do you need to be successful?

Our ideal candidate looks like this:
Proven track record as a Network Engineer in high-availability environments;
Strong troubleshooting skills and the ability to remediate complex network and security issues;
Hands-on experience with Cisco, Arista, and/or Extreme Networks;
Expertise with F5, Cisco ASA and Palo Alto;
Experience with automation and Infra as Code, like Terraform, Ansible, Chef;
Familiarity with public cloud networking (Azure) and integrating with on-premises environments.
Fluency in both Dutch and English language.

If you want to work on large, complex projects designing and developing mission-critical infrastructures whilst also working on focus on existing network environments, this is the role for you.

Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.

It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.

